FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://api.example.com

# Schemas Demo

A small APIB exercising resource-level + Attributes (default response
schema), action-level + Attributes (default request schema), inline
+ Attributes overriding both, and a raw + Schema block (highest priority).

## Item [/items/{id}]

+ Parameters
    + id (number, required) - Item identifier

+ Attributes (object)
    + id: 42 (number, required) - Resource identifier
    + name: widget (string, required) - Display name

### Get Item [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body

            { "id": 42, "name": "widget" }

### Update Item [PATCH]

+ Attributes (object)
    + name (string, required)
    + active (boolean)

+ Request (application/json)

    + Body

            { "active": true, "name": "thing" }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body

            { "active": true, "id": 42, "name": "thing" }

### Delete Item [DELETE]

+ Response 204

## Replace [/replace]

### Replace [POST]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Attributes (object)
        + alpha (string, required)
        + beta (number)

    + Body

            { "alpha": "x" }

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body

            { "ok": true }

